From 2a2c3ea55b64b23f25ff4223410de561eb2c90b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:47:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: use MCP tools so per-user aim_ keys work

Once an ai-memory server has users, every /admin/* route is root-only. The
plugin called /admin/search, /admin/write-page and /admin/status, so recall
and writes answered 403 to anything but the root token while /hook and
/handoff kept working. Verified against a real ai-memory 2.5.2 server with a
user and aim_ keys (before: 403 on status, write and search; after: all pass).

- search: memory_query over POST /mcp (global=true when no scope), falling
  back to GET /admin/search only when the server has no /mcp route
- write_page: memory_write_page over POST /mcp, same fallback
- status: /admin/status, then memory_status on 403; the CLI reports it
- /api/v1 is not used: it only exists when the server runs with --enable-web
- strip FTS5 <mark> markers from snippets
- send workspace/project only as a pair
- merge request headers case-insensitively (Accept was sent twice)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0138yoe5oowW63pzPUPYnYS6
