diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 1309cf2..178c985 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -28,6 +28,11 @@
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- **Per-user keys (`aim_`) no longer get 403 on recall and writes.** Once an ai-memory server has users, every `/admin/*` route is root-only, and the plugin used `/admin/search`, `/admin/write-page` and `/admin/status`, so only the shared root token worked while `/hook` and `/handoff` kept working, which made the failure look partial. `search()` now calls the `memory_query` MCP tool, `write_page()` calls `memory_write_page`, and `status()` falls back to `memory_status` when `/admin/status` answers 403, all over `POST /mcp`. A server with no `/mcp` route (404/405) still falls back to the `/admin` routes once, then stays on them for the life of the client. The read-only `/api/v1` routes are not used: they only exist when the server runs with `--enable-web`.
+- Search snippets carry FTS5 `<mark>` markers; they are stripped before the hit reaches a prompt.
+- `write_page()` sends `workspace` and `project` only as a pair (a static MCP client must name both; one alone is rejected).
+- `AiMemoryClient._request` merged caller headers into a plain dict, so a caller's `Accept` was sent next to the client default `accept: */*`. It now merges case-insensitively.
+
 - `AiMemoryProvider.queue_prefetch()` now accepts the `session_id` keyword Hermes passes (`MemoryManager.queue_prefetch_all`), so the background recall actually runs and the next turn's `prefetch()` is a cache read. Results are cached per `(session_id, query)` and consumed once.
 - `AiMemoryProvider.on_memory_write()` now mirrors `add` and `replace` — the actions Hermes announces (its `_MIRRORED_MEMORY_ACTIONS`). The old `write`/`append` gate matched nothing, so no built-in `MEMORY.md` / `USER.md` write was ever mirrored; `write`/`append` stay accepted as synonyms for older callers. A `replace` keeps the superseded entry under `## Substituído`, and `remove` is skipped.
 - The tool schemas now use the `parameters` key Hermes normalizes (`MemoryProvider.get_tool_schemas`) instead of `input_schema`, which reached the model as a function with no argument list.
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2a0bbec..f65c20b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -119,6 +119,21 @@ hermes ai-memory config-set auth_token my-secret
 #   export AI_MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN='my-secret'
 ```
 
+## Credentials and server access
+
+The plugin works with the root `AI_MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN` and with a per-user `aim_` key
+(`ai-memory api-key add --username <user> --label <node>`). A per-user key is the better
+choice on a shared server: it attributes every write, can be revoked on its own, and handoffs
+stay owned by that user, so give every node of one person a key for the same user.
+
+| Plugin call | Route | Needs |
+|---|---|---|
+| recall / `ai_memory_search` | MCP `memory_query` over `POST /mcp` (falls back to `GET /admin/search` on servers without `/mcp`) | any valid key |
+| `ai_memory_write` and memory mirroring | MCP `memory_write_page` over `POST /mcp` (falls back to `POST /admin/write-page`) | any valid key |
+| turn capture, session end | `POST /hook` | any valid key |
+| handoff | `GET /handoff` | any valid key |
+| `hermes ai-memory status` | `GET /admin/status`, then MCP `memory_status` on 403 | root for version and counters |
+
 ## Tools
 
 | Tool | Description | Parameters |
